9. ORDER AND TABLE SESSION BUSINESS LOGIC
The system must handle multiple orders within the same active table session.
Example:
Table 5:
•	First order: Beef Burger + Coca Cola.
•	Second order: Fried Rice.
•	Third order: Spring Rolls.
All orders must belong to the correct active table session.
The checkout screen must calculate the unpaid balance for that session without accidentally charging previously paid orders again.
Important rules:
•	Never create duplicate orders from repeated submissions.
•	Never allow an order for an inactive table.
•	Prevent unauthorized table-session changes.
•	Maintain order and payment history.
•	Do not close a table session while unpaid balances remain.
•	Do not change completed payment records without an auditable adjustment process.
